Partial agree: the comment was wrong, the implementation was right. Fixed in c5b912a9. Empty `{}` is intentionally a no-op (PATCH convention — empty patch should preserve state). Only an explicit `null` for the whole field clears every override. Comment now reflects this:

```
// PATCH semantics:
//   • null            → clear every per-window override on this connection
//   • {} (empty map)  → no-op (no keys to merge); existing overrides preserved
//   • partial map     → merge into the existing map; a `null` value at any
//                        key clears just that window's override
```

If you want "clear all" you send `{ "quotaWindowThresholds": null }`, not `{ "quotaWindowThresholds": {} }`.

